-- title:
--   Elements normalising an Eichler order normalise its Fuchsian group
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \neq 0$ and primes $q, q'$ with $q' \neq q$, neither dividing $N$, and rationals $a, b$ such that the quaternion algebra $B = \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`: $a > 0$ or $b > 0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completion $B \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ has every nonzero element invertible precisely when $q \in v$ or $q' \in v$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $B$ that is a maximal order (an order in the sense of containing $1$, closed under multiplication, finitely generated and $\mathbb{Q}$-spanning $B$, and maximal among such), let $N$ be squarefree, and let $R \leq \Lambda$ be an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R = \Lambda_1 \cap \Lambda_2$ for maximal orders $\Lambda_i$ with the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ equal to $N$. Let $\iota : B \to M_2(\mathbb{R})$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map, and let $w \in B^{\times}$ satisfy $\mathrm{nrd}(w) > 0$ and $x \in R \iff w x w^{-1} \in R$ for all $x \in B$. Then there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ whose underlying matrix is $\iota(w)$, with $\det g > 0$, such that for every $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ one has $\gamma \in \Gamma_R \iff g\gamma g^{-1} \in \Gamma_R$, where $\Gamma_R =$ `fuchsianGroup R ι` is the image under $\iota$ of the subgroup of $B^{\times}$ generated by the units lying in $R$ together with a two-sided inverse in $R$, intersected with the kernel of the determinant; moreover every $u \in R$ having a two-sided inverse in $R$ and $\mathrm{nrd}(u) = 1$ equals $\iota$ of (the matrix of) some element of $\Gamma_R$, and $\mathrm{nrd}(w x w^{-1}) = \mathrm{nrd}(x)$ for all $x \in B$.
--
--   This is the elementary step underlying the Atkin–Lehner action on Shimura curves attached to indefinite quaternion algebras: an element of $B^{\times}$ of positive reduced norm normalising the Eichler order $R$ induces, through a real splitting $\iota$, an element of $\mathrm{GL}_2^{+}(\mathbb{R})$ normalising the associated Fuchsian group. It is used in the comparison of Atkin–Lehner twists of period lattices with Hecke data at the level $N$ in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd part of the argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_exists_gl_conj_fuchsianGroup_iff_of_forall_mem_iff_conj_mem.lean

